<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Deutsche Telekom given Kazakh deal deadline.</title>
<headline>Deutsche Telekom given Kazakh deal deadline.</headline>
<byline>Larisa Kokovinets</byline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Deutsche Telekom AG has until the end of December to take up a 49 percent share in Kazakhstan's state telecoms monopoly or face losing the 825 million mark deal, a senior Kazakh official said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;If the contract is not signed by 31 December 1996, then the deal is anulled,&quot; Sarybai Kalmurzayev, the powerful head of Kazakhstan's State Property Committee, told Reuters in an interview in the capital Almaty.</p>
</text>
